<Legal
  title="Preview Privacy"
  description="What Volli’s invite-only cloud preview stores, who processes it, and how to request access or deletion."
  path="/legal/privacy/"
>
  <p>
    This page covers the invite-only Volli 0.3 cloud preview and our website and docs.
    Volli is operated by Hussain Phalasiya in Ontario, Canada. For privacy questions,
    access, correction, export or deletion requests, email
    <a href="mailto:privacy@volli.app">privacy@volli.app</a>. For support, email
    <a href="mailto:support@volli.app">support@volli.app</a>. Do not post personal data
    or private code in a public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>What the preview handles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account and access:</strong> your name, email, sign-in identity and session
      information from the sign-in service, invitation eligibility, and the version and
      time of your Preview Agreement acceptance.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Workspace data:</strong> Workspace and project details, membership, invitations
      and sponsorship records, tickets, comments, Automations, settings, attachments and
      Session history. History includes prompts, model responses, tool calls and results,
      and agent logs; it can contain source code, file contents, paths, personal information
      or secrets encountered by an agent. Moving a local project to the cloud also uploads
      its exported records, history, logs and attachments through staging storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connections and stored credentials:</strong> API keys, secrets or integration
      credentials you choose to store as cloud secrets, and connected-account metadata.
      Connecting a model on your Mac does not by itself upload its key. If you connect
      GitHub, we store profile, verified email, repository and installation information,
      and authorization tokens. These are separate from subscription logins kept on your machine.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service and support data:</strong> device and runner connection information,
      app version, sign-in and security records, service errors, and anything you choose
      to send us for support. Website and service requests expose connection information
      such as IP addresses and browser details to the providers handling them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this data to authenticate you, control preview access, sync your work, operate
    and secure the service, respond to support and privacy requests, and comply with law.
    We do not sell personal data, use your content for advertising, or use it to train AI models.
  </p>

  <h2>Local tools do not mean local history</h2>
  <p>
    In signed-out local mode, your board and Session history are stored on your device.
    Cloud Workspaces and their history sync through our cloud backend. Signing in alone
    does not move existing local projects; a move is a separate action. An
    agent running on your Mac can put file contents and command output into that history.
    Treat a synced Session as sensitive as the material it reads. Avoid submitting secrets
    or sensitive or regulated personal data; do not assume redaction catches everything.
  </p>
  <p>
    In this preview, model requests go from the machine running the agent to the model provider or gateway
    you choose, under your agreement with it. They include prompts, code context and tool
    results. The preview does not route model calls through a Volli-operated model gateway.
    Subscription credentials are used only on the machine where you sign in to the provider.
    Cloud history still stores prompts and responses even though the model call is direct.
    MCP servers, web tools and other services you use can also receive the data you or an
    agent sends them. They have their own privacy practices. Signed-out mode does not stop
    those requests or app update checks. Our download page requests release information
    from GitHub in your browser, and app update checks and downloads contact GitHub Releases.
    GitHub receives connection information for these requests under its own privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can receive data</h2>
  <p>
    Our preview service providers are <strong>Convex, Cloudflare, WorkOS and Google Workspace</strong>.
    Convex stores account, board and Session records; Cloudflare R2 holds uploaded history,
    attachments and move staging; WorkOS handles sign-in; Google Workspace handles emails
    you send us and our replies. See
    <a href="/legal/subprocessors/">their roles and the data they process</a>. Data may be
    processed outside Canada, including in the United States and on global networks,
    under different laws. We do not promise Canadian-only storage.
  </p>
  <p>
    Other Workspace members can see work shared with them; ticket work is shared by
    default. Ad-hoc chats and Board Sessions start private, but their owner can share them, and a Workspace
    administrator can make all Sessions shared. Sharing a Session cannot be undone in the
    preview and also shares its private subagents. Leaving a Workspace does not erase
    contributions already stored in it. We may access data as needed for support, service
    operation, security or legal requirements, and disclose data when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and credentials</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud connections use HTTPS/TLS. <a href="https://www.convex.dev/security">Convex</a>
    and <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/reference/data-security/">Cloudflare R2</a>
    describe encryption in transit and at rest for the data they host. This is not
    end-to-end encryption: our service and its providers can process readable content.
    Cloud secrets are separately encrypted under service-held keys; ordinary environment
    variables are not secret values. Provider API keys and subscription credentials saved
    by Pi stay in an owner-only local credential file, not encrypted by Volli. They are
    used locally to authenticate to your provider, not uploaded to Volli Cloud. Your Volli
    account refresh token is separate: the desktop stores it in a sealed local store with
    a key wrapped through the macOS keychain. These protections do not prevent secrets
    appearing in prompts or tool output.
  </p>
  <p>
    No system can guarantee perfect security or confidentiality. Report vulnerabilities
    privately to <a href="mailto:security@volli.app">security@volli.app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional telemetry</h2>
  <p>
    This preview has no Volli-operated product analytics or crash-reporting integration.
    Accepting the Preview Agreement does not opt you into one. We will update this notice
    and the provider list before introducing one, with any required notice or choice.
    Operational records needed to run and secure the service are separate. Agent telemetry
    is off until you enable it in Settings and supply a collector; that collector receives
    the events you enable for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
  <p>
    We retain account and Workspace data to operate the preview; there is no automatic
    expiry for cloud project history. This is not a promise of permanent storage: preview
    data may be lost or reset. Keep independent copies of work you cannot lose. Local
    profile backups are not backups of your live cloud Workspace, and we do not guarantee
    cloud backup frequency, recovery time or recoverability during this preview.
  </p>
  <p>
    Settings → Account lets you request account deletion and cancel the request within
    30 days. The request blocks normal cloud access, but the automatic account-data purge
    is not implemented in this preview. The 30 days is a cancellation window, not a promise
    to erase all data by day 30. A sole owner of a Workspace with other active members must
    transfer ownership before requesting deletion. Requesting deletion disconnects GitHub
    and revokes cloud device sessions; cancelling does not reconnect them. After the
    cancellation window ends, contact us for help; do not assume erasure has completed.
    Archiving a project or ticket hides it;
    it does not purge its history. There is no complete self-service cloud project or
    Workspace deletion or export yet. Contact
    <a href="mailto:privacy@volli.app">privacy@volli.app</a> for help with these requests.
    We may need to verify your identity and involve a shared Workspace's owner.
  </p>
  <p>
    Moving a project back to local does not delete its cloud copy. Cancelling an unfinished
    move schedules removal of that move's imported rows and uploaded objects; failures can
    delay cleanup. We have not verified automatic expiry of move-staging uploads and do
    not promise a 7-day or 30-day removal deadline. Deleted material may also remain in
    backups and service records; we do not promise a fixed backup purge deadline. We may
    retain records for security or legal obligations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or receive
    a portable copy of your data, object to or restrict processing, withdraw consent, or
    complain to a privacy regulator. Contact us to exercise those rights; preview feature
    limitations do not limit them. Uninstalling or deleting local app data does not delete
    cloud data or copies held by your model providers and other services.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will publish an updated version here before materially changing these practices
    and require acceptance of the current Preview Agreement before further cloud access.
    This preview is intended for software development, not for children's use. If you
    believe a child has provided personal data, contact
    <a href="mailto:privacy@volli.app">privacy@volli.app</a> so we can address it.
  </p>
</Legal>
